<!-- Public pages only, and the omissions are deliberate rather than
     accidental — checked page by page on 2026-08-21 against which files
     actually carry a robots meta tag.

     ABSENT ON PURPOSE, all carrying <meta name="robots" content="noindex">:
     the re-engagement tool and its checks, the session-contract checks, the
     synthetic studio generator and its checks, and the readiness board.
     They are left crawlable so that tag is read and honoured, which is the
     only guaranteed way to stay out of an index.

     ABSENT AND SHOULD NOT BE: the staff scheduling dashboard and its
     second page carry NO robots tag at all, so nothing keeps their roster
     and attendance content out of an index. Listing them here would make
     that worse, so they stay out — but leaving them out is not protection.
     The fix is one meta tag in their owner's lane; see
     docs/REQUESTFOR-A-B-C.md.

     storytold.html was missing from this file until 2026-08-21. It is
     public, carries no noindex, and is linked from the front door's
     footer — so it was indexable and simply unlisted.

     The terms and the privacy policy are listed on purpose. They are the
     two pages a person looks for BY NAME, often from a search rather than
     from the footer, and a legal page nobody can find is a legal page
     nobody has been given. settings.html is the opposite case and carries
     noindex: it is a control, not something to read. -->
